From bb57afa2f8c5a9b3aa6939fc4501f6b548848557 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:32:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Ghost expiry keeps a remote chat link until its
 owner row verifies the completion

A reprovisioned Board worker restores its cards from the Board, but not
kanban_notify_subs. The hub collector builds a task's `sessions` from
that table only, so the worker republished every pre-reprovision card
with `sessions: []`. `_legacy_remote_links` treated the dropped link on a
present owner row as a ghost and expired the retained snapshot row, and
the origin's chat-link reconcile then released the link. On the hub
(2026-11-11 22:26:35Z) that released six shepherd links of one chat in a
single batch. Three of those cards were still open (scheduled, todo,
ready), and one done card had origin_observation.verified=false.

Ghost expiry now needs the fresh owner record for the card's exact
(gateway, profile, board, id) to be owner-attested terminal (fresh
scope heartbeat, hash-bound observation) and verified, the
`_verified_terminal` predicate. `_read_remote_links` (both the full
and the incremental projection, and the memo) reports these records
as `closed_out`. An open row, or a closed row without verified
completion, keeps the retained row as a stale unfinished obligation, so
the link stays wanted and unreleased. NULL profiles never match a
qualified record. The receipt-backed terminal-carry predicates and the
missing-open-obligation selector are unchanged. The producer side
(sessions not restored) is a separate follow-up card.

Proof:
- RED: the new test_kanban_ghost_expiry_open_obligation.py had 18 of 20
  failing on the unchanged base (open x5 and unverified done/archived,
  each on the incremental and full-read paths, plus another profile's
  verified row and reopen-then-verified). Verified done passed before
  and after the fix.
- GREEN: all 102 test files that import the touched modules pass, except
  2 tests in test_web_links_stale.py that fail the same way on the
  unmodified base.
- 8/8 condition mutants are killed: the verified gate on both paths,
  discard on row change, memo store and memo hit, exact profile key,
  filter dropped, and the attest/fresh gate.
